<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Emperor Bing of Song</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1272">1272</a>–<a href="/years/1279">1279</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Zhao Bing</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Emperor Bing of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song</a>, personal name Zhao Bing, was the last emperor of the Song dynasty, enthroned as a child in 1278 by loyalists fleeing the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a> along the southern coast. When the Yuan fleet destroyed the Song navy at Yamen in March 1279, the minister <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lu-xiufu">Lu Xiufu</a> leapt into the sea with the seven-year-old emperor on his back, and both drowned, ending the dynasty.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>A loyalist fleet of more than a thousand ships was destroyed, and the minister Lu Xiufu leapt into the sea carrying the last Song emperor, the seven-year-old <b>Zhao Bing</b>; many officials followed them.</blockquote><a href="/empire/song-dynasty">Song Dynasty · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hangzhou">Hangzhou</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/china">China</a>. Died in Yamen, in what is now <a href="/countries/china">China</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=30.25,120.17&amp;year=1276" aria-label="Hangzhou on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7669 1060 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Emperor Bing of Song"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M8119 1330h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M8119 1330h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=30.25,120.17&amp;year=1276">What was here in 1276? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
